preConditionHook:
// WHERE THE CLOSING PRICE SITS IN THE DAY'S RANGE SO FAR. At strengthMode = 0 (the
// default, and the original rule) the long side wants the close in the BOTTOM
// nearExtremeFraction of the range -- the FADE read, which is how Brooks states
// it for trading-range days -- and the short the top fraction. V25-01 states it
// as a block ("do not buy near the top of the day's range") and RP4-21 as a
// permission (look for a reversal at the day's extreme going into the last hour
// or two); one is the other flipped, so they are one rule.
//
// AT strengthMode != 0 THE TWO SIDES SWAP: the long wants the close in the TOP
// fraction, the STRENGTH read (added 2026-09-22 for the A-list
// CloseInTopOfSessionRange, G08-26). Grimes's own 80/20 thresholds are this
// rule at strengthMode = 1 and nearExtremeFraction = 0.2, because
// close - sessLow >= 0.8 * range IS sessHigh - close <= 0.2 * range. Same
// statistic, opposite polarity, and the per-placement negate toggle gives
// "not A", never the mirror side (merge decision 12) -- which is why this is a
// boolean input and not a second file. At the default 0, longGap and shortGap
// are the original two expressions and nearBand the original right-hand side,
// computed in the same order, so nothing changes by a single bar.
//
// RP4-21's final-hours term is the catalog's TimeWindow ANDed alongside and is
// not carried here; V25-01's day-type gate is TradingRangeDay, likewise a
// separate pane.
//
// Kept apart from RangeExtremeFade and CloseInRangePosition because the
// window is the SESSION, not a bar count -- early in a session the day's
// range is a handful of bars and late in one it may be wider than any 20-bar
// window, so the two disagree constantly. Not CloseNearSessionRangeMidpoint,
// which bands the MIDDLE of the same window and is direction-agnostic. Not
// SessionOpenPositionInRange, which places the session's OPENING price in the
// same window.
//
// Written MULTIPLIED, never as a ratio, so a session whose high equals its
// low fires on both sides rather than raising EL's runtime divide-by-zero.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the twin's date > date[1],
// mirrored as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)), with the running
// extremes held in locals reset on that change. Intraday bars only. On the
// session's first bar sessHigh/sessLow are that bar's own extremes, so the
// test degenerates to CloseRangePosition on that bar alone.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 1.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    sessHigh = high[0];
    sessLow = low[0];
} else {
    if (el_gt(high[0], sessHigh)) sessHigh = high[0];
    if (el_lt(low[0], sessLow)) sessLow = low[0];
}
nearBand = nearExtremeFraction * (sessHigh - sessLow);
if (el_eq(strengthMode, 0.0)) {
    longGap = close[0] - sessLow;
    shortGap = sessHigh - close[0];
} else {
    longGap = sessHigh - close[0];
    shortGap = close[0] - sessLow;
}
